We want a transformation matrix that maps any vector $(x, y)$ to $(0, y)$. This is a linear transformation, so we can represent it with a matrix multiplication. 

Let's denote the projection matrix as $P$. Then, for any vector $\mathbf{v} = \begin{bmatrix} x \\ y \end{bmatrix}$, we have 

$$ P \mathbf{v} = \begin{bmatrix} 0 \\ y \end{bmatrix} $$

